 Interview Experience – Persistent Systems (Face to Face) 🚀

face-to-face interview with Persistent Systems, which consisted of two rounds:

🔹 Round 1 – Online Test (25 minutes, 20 questions)

 The test was hands-on troubleshooting + multiple-choice questions, covering:

AWS & DevOps (4 questions) – scenario-based MCQs
Jenkins (4 questions) – identify errors in pipeline code snippets
Docker (4 questions) – debug Dockerfile & analyze logs to find root causes
Kubernetes (4 questions) – check manifests/screenshots and identify errors
Terraform (4 questions) – troubleshoot IaC code with scenario-based problems

This round was not just about theoretical knowledge but more about practical debugging skills.

🔹 Round 2 – Technical Interview (1 hr 20 mins)
 This was an in-depth discussion across multiple DevOps tools & practices. Some of the key scenario-based questions were:

AWS
Troubleshooting EC2 Auto Scaling latency issues
Designing multi-region DR with RTO < 15 mins & RPO < 5 mins
Fixing session management issues behind ALB during traffic spikes
Securing S3 logs with encryption & monitoring
VPC connectivity troubleshooting (private subnets & internet access)

Jenkins
Optimizing pipelines with parallel & distributed builds
Securing pipelines using AWS Secrets Manager / Vault
Designing resilient Jenkins master-agent architecture
Implementing zero-downtime deployments (Blue/Green, Canary)

Docker
Debugging OOMKilled / memory leaks
Fixing networking errors in production
Optimizing Dockerfile for faster, smaller builds
Managing base images securely across environments

Kubernetes (K8s + Helm)
Troubleshooting CrashLoopBackOff pods
Designing zero-downtime rollouts (Blue/Green, ArgoCD with Helm)
NetworkPolicy debugging for cross-namespace communication
Handling failed Helm upgrades & rollbacks
Setting up HPA/VPA for OOMKilled & CPU throttling

Prometheus & Grafana
Tuning alert rules & scraping frequency
Designing HA Prometheus + Grafana setup
Collecting custom business metrics for observability
Optimizing query performance & storage during peak load

Dynatrace
Using PurePath & Service Flow for root-cause tracing
Reconciling CloudWatch vs Dynatrace metrics
Designing multi-cloud unified observability dashboards

💡 Key Takeaway:
 This interview experience was a true test of hands-on troubleshooting, observability, and designing resilient architectures across the DevOps ecosystem. 

